1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:01,350
(All characters and organizations in this drama are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,350 --> 00:00:02,390
(Filming with minors followed broadcast guidelines,)

3
00:00:02,390 --> 00:00:03,420
(and generative AI was used in select scenes.)

4
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:05,520
I loved him.

5
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:08,020
I loved him, but...

6
00:00:08,490 --> 00:00:09,790
I mean, it would be one thing if I hadn't known,

7
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:11,990
but I knew exactly what family he came from.

8
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:14,220
A penniless day laborer like Kim Mu Jin.

9
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:16,320
What's so appealing about that to me now?

10
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:17,820
If things stay as they are,

11
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,690
I'd have to take on all of Kim Mu Jin's burdens...

12
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:22,020
without any help from you.

13
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:24,120
Honestly, I'm not confident I can do that.

14
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:26,820
We only dated for one year.

15
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:29,050
And we're not married.

16
00:00:29,490 --> 00:00:31,950
I'm having a hard enough time as it is.

17
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:34,820
How am I supposed to know...

18
00:00:34,890 --> 00:00:36,490
how bad his disability from the crash will be?

19
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:39,490
I can't do it. I don't want to.

20
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:40,820
Are you...

21
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,590
even human?

22
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:43,820
Are you?

23
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:49,120
Because of a pathetic girl like you, my Mu Jin...

24
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:56,090
What is this?

25
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:57,220
Mu Jin...

26
00:00:57,750 --> 00:00:59,820
is not the kind of person who gives up on me easily.

27
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:03,650
This is what it would take for him to finally give up on me.

28
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:10,090
I'm sorry to have caused you this unnecessary worry.

29
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:11,490
The 100,000 dollars...

30
00:01:12,390 --> 00:01:13,650
Do you still need the money?

31
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:15,920
I don't need it.

32
00:01:36,590 --> 00:01:38,020
(Episode 11)

33
00:01:53,490 --> 00:01:57,650
By any chance, did you go to Duwon Girls' Middle School?

34
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:03,150
- Lim Hye Jeong? - Han Gyu Rim?

35
00:02:03,990 --> 00:02:05,220
Oh my gosh.

36
00:02:06,090 --> 00:02:10,020
- It's been so long. - How long has it been?

37
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:11,720
Is this our first time seeing each other since middle school?

38
00:02:11,790 --> 00:02:13,550
Fancy meeting you here.

39
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:16,150
I know. Of all people,

40
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:18,650
I've been hoping to run into you, Gyu Rim.

41
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:21,950
Me too. I've missed you so much.

42
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:24,790
Are you about to give birth too?

43
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:30,020
I hadn't heard you got married.

44
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:34,290
Are you here with your husband? What's he like?

45
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:38,550
I'm not married.

46
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,090
This baby...

47
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:46,590
is just mine.

48
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,220
Just a little more.

49
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:56,750
Just a little more.

50
00:03:00,190 --> 00:03:01,950
Just a little more effort.

51
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:03,290
You're almost there.

52
00:03:14,690 --> 00:03:16,020
Where is my baby?

53
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:21,550
Why isn't my baby...

54
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:24,820
Why can't I hear my baby crying?

55
00:03:25,590 --> 00:03:26,950
During the delivery,

56
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:29,250
there was an issue with the baby's heartbeat.

57
00:03:29,650 --> 00:03:31,820
We did everything we could,

58
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:34,450
but I'm so sorry.

59
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:36,390
Are you...

60
00:03:38,290 --> 00:03:39,520
saying my baby...

61
00:03:42,950 --> 00:03:44,450
is dead?

62
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:47,990
Is that what you're telling me?

63
00:04:19,950 --> 00:04:22,620
(Mom)

64
00:04:28,390 --> 00:04:29,390
Hello?

65
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:33,120
Is this Go Yoon Hee's phone?

66
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:35,820
Yes, it is. Who's calling?

67
00:04:37,950 --> 00:04:39,490
It's Gyu Rim.

68
00:04:42,090 --> 00:04:43,190
Mom.

69
00:04:44,550 --> 00:04:46,850
I heard you remarried.

70
00:04:48,690 --> 00:04:50,890
You seem to be doing well,

71
00:04:52,550 --> 00:04:54,350
so I wasn't going to call.

72
00:04:59,850 --> 00:05:02,050
It's just...

73
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:05,790
that I miss you so much, Mom.

74
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,120
I'm...

75
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:19,820
going through a really, really hard time.

76
00:05:21,390 --> 00:05:23,950
Can you please come to me right now?

77
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:28,020
Just this once.

78
00:05:30,550 --> 00:05:32,020
Please, just this one time.

79
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,950
It's been a while, Gyu Rim.

80
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:40,390
I'm sorry...

81
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:43,350
that I haven't been in touch.

82
00:05:46,450 --> 00:05:47,620
But...

83
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:50,290
Right now...

84
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:56,820
My daughter had an appendectomy today,

85
00:05:57,250 --> 00:05:59,350
so I can't really go anywhere for a while.

86
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:01,720
Mom.

87
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,050
Seo Hyun, you're awake?

88
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:06,990
I'm sorry.

89
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:09,920
Things are just crazy right now...

90
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:12,990
I'll call you back later.

91
00:06:13,990 --> 00:06:15,220
I'm sorry.

92
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:24,650
What do I do?

93
00:06:32,790 --> 00:06:34,820
What do I do?

94
00:06:36,390 --> 00:06:38,150
I just remembered.

95
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:43,490
Now I know what I lost.

96
00:06:44,790 --> 00:06:47,920
I remember now. What do I do?

97
00:06:50,790 --> 00:06:54,350
A long time ago, I lost so much.

98
00:06:56,590 --> 00:06:57,590
My mother,

99
00:06:58,990 --> 00:07:00,020
my baby,

100
00:07:01,690 --> 00:07:02,820
and Kim Mu Jin.

101
00:07:05,490 --> 00:07:07,450
I'd even forgotten that I'd lost them...

102
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:09,550
and just kept on living.

103
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:14,150
I thought I was doing okay.

104
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:18,350
So why is it all coming back to me now?

105
00:07:35,890 --> 00:07:37,350
I want to help you find it,

106
00:07:38,850 --> 00:07:40,550
but I think I have to go now.

107
00:07:49,590 --> 00:07:50,750
I'm sorry...

108
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,490
for running away...

109
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:57,690
I'm sorry...

110
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:02,450
for giving up.

111
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:06,520
I'm sorry...

112
00:08:11,590 --> 00:08:12,920
for losing you.

113
00:08:17,590 --> 00:08:18,790
What you lost...

114
00:08:21,990 --> 00:08:23,150
was me?

115
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,150
Will I ever be able to find...

116
00:08:38,150 --> 00:08:39,760
what I've lost?

117
00:08:44,650 --> 00:08:46,450
I'm sorry I lied.

118
00:08:47,950 --> 00:08:49,320
I'm sorry for lying to myself...

119
00:08:50,190 --> 00:08:51,690
and to you.

120
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:57,490
I'm so sorry, Mu Jin.

121
00:08:58,890 --> 00:09:02,150
I'm so sorry.

122
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:08,690
If only you'd remembered a little sooner...

123
00:09:12,390 --> 00:09:14,220
If only I'd found you a little faster...

124
00:09:28,090 --> 00:09:29,390
I'm sorry, Gyu Rim.

125
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:32,690
I can't...

126
00:09:34,650 --> 00:09:36,190
go back to you.

127
00:09:40,590 --> 00:09:41,650
I...

128
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,790
I've met someone else.

129
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:57,220
Someone who will love you as much as I did...

130
00:09:58,990 --> 00:10:00,190
will come along.

131
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:04,150
Someone you can love again...

132
00:10:05,990 --> 00:10:07,190
will come along.

133
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:11,850
When that happens, don't give up.

134
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:14,590
Don't be afraid.

135
00:10:16,190 --> 00:10:17,450
Don't run away.

136
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,320
And don't lose that person.

137
00:10:24,650 --> 00:10:25,650
Take care.

138
00:10:27,390 --> 00:10:28,390
And stay well.

139
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:10,620
Gyu Rim.

140
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:12,650
Han Gyu Rim.

141
00:11:13,450 --> 00:11:14,450
Hey.

142
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:17,220
Come on, snap out of it.

143
00:11:18,790 --> 00:11:21,690
Hey, you got your cast off. Are you okay now?

144
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:23,220
Of course I'm okay.

145
00:11:23,620 --> 00:11:24,920
I shouldn't have made such a fuss...

146
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,520
about wearing a cast from the beginning.

147
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:30,350
But hey, are you okay?

148
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:34,420
It's only been a week, but you look so worn out.

149
00:11:40,850 --> 00:11:44,490
I'm not going to see you as a man or woman anymore.

150
00:11:45,190 --> 00:11:46,250
What...

151
00:11:47,050 --> 00:11:48,320
What do you mean by that?

152
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,320
I'm sorry...

153
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:53,250
for being so indecisive and going back and forth.

154
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,450
I'm awful, aren't I?

155
00:12:01,850 --> 00:12:04,250
Why don't you just hit me?

156
00:12:06,590 --> 00:12:10,390
If you want to hit me until you're not angry anymore, go ahead.

157
00:12:26,390 --> 00:12:27,490
I'm okay now.

158
00:12:28,690 --> 00:12:32,550
I can breathe properly, and my heart isn't pounding.

159
00:12:36,650 --> 00:12:37,650
So you're not going to hit me?

160
00:12:38,950 --> 00:12:41,290
Where would I even hit you?

161
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:43,550
If I so much as flicked you with my finger,

162
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:45,350
you look like you'd fly all the way to Jeju Island.

163
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:49,020
I'm sorry.

164
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:51,320
That I proposed to you,

165
00:12:56,090 --> 00:12:57,090
I'm taking it back.

166
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:00,220
Is that so?

167
00:13:04,790 --> 00:13:06,720
Right. You made a good decision.

168
00:13:07,050 --> 00:13:09,050
To be honest, whenever you came close,

169
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:10,750
I felt like I was going to die.

170
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:13,250
It's not like I'm fighting for our country's independence,

171
00:13:13,550 --> 00:13:15,190
so I figured it wasn't worth risking my life over.

172
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:19,550
I was going to turn you down first.

173
00:13:21,390 --> 00:13:22,620
Don't forgive me.

174
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:25,250
Okay.

175
00:13:26,590 --> 00:13:30,290
I won't forgive you, so let's start a kitty instead.

176
00:13:31,190 --> 00:13:32,850
We can each put in 30 dollars a month...

177
00:13:32,850 --> 00:13:34,150
for chicken and beer.

178
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:36,590
As a big brother and little sister, okay?

179
00:13:42,290 --> 00:13:44,450
You haven't told my mom yet, have you?

180
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:49,390
I was going to tell her after seeing you.

181
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:52,020
No. Absolutely not.

182
00:13:52,550 --> 00:13:54,550
You're saying that because you don't really know my mom.

183
00:13:55,350 --> 00:13:59,490
Just say that I, Heung Sik, broke it all off.

184
00:13:59,550 --> 00:14:00,690
Just put all the blame on me.

185
00:14:01,390 --> 00:14:02,620
Got it?

186
00:14:03,150 --> 00:14:04,350
Okay?

187
00:14:04,450 --> 00:14:06,820
What did you just say?

188
00:14:08,450 --> 00:14:09,590
What was that?

189
00:14:10,050 --> 00:14:13,720
You proposed to my Heung Sik,

190
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:16,190
but you want to take it back.

191
00:14:16,390 --> 00:14:19,520
You're saying you want to pretend it never happened?

192
00:14:22,190 --> 00:14:23,590
I'm sorry, Ma'am.

193
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:38,520
I feel like a frog about to be killed...

194
00:14:38,590 --> 00:14:40,220
by a stone you just threw.

195
00:14:40,290 --> 00:14:42,990
"I'm sorry"? Is that all it takes?

196
00:14:43,490 --> 00:14:46,290
My Heung Sik and I were so taken with you.

197
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:47,850
Even though you're a single mother,

198
00:14:48,050 --> 00:14:51,250
we were dancing for joy, not caring that you were poor.

199
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:54,290
Did you think we were a couple of pushovers?

200
00:14:55,650 --> 00:14:57,290
That's not true, Ma'am.

201
00:14:58,020 --> 00:15:02,750
Do you think I was out of my mind to like a flawed woman like you?

202
00:15:02,950 --> 00:15:05,890
No way.

203
00:15:06,590 --> 00:15:08,550
A good shaman on Dobongsan told me...

204
00:15:08,890 --> 00:15:12,520
that my Heung Sik was fated to have a sudden death.

205
00:15:13,450 --> 00:15:17,450
He had to marry a widow with a child or a flawed woman...

206
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:19,720
to get rid of that bad luck.

207
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,690
How dare you?

208
00:15:21,850 --> 00:15:25,450
I was going to accept you when my son has never married.

209
00:15:25,450 --> 00:15:26,520
Got it?

210
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:27,990
My, my.

211
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:30,720
Now that I think about it,

212
00:15:31,050 --> 00:15:35,020
did Gyeol's Dad come find you?

213
00:15:35,620 --> 00:15:37,550
Did he convince you three to make a go of it...

214
00:15:37,890 --> 00:15:40,390
after you dump my Heung Sik?

215
00:15:40,590 --> 00:15:44,220
- Is that what happened? - Gyeol has no father, Ma'am.

216
00:15:45,890 --> 00:15:47,590
To you and Heung Sik,

217
00:15:48,490 --> 00:15:50,220
I just don't want to make any more mistakes...

218
00:15:50,290 --> 00:15:54,320
- Make mistakes until you die. - Ma'am.

219
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:57,750
Enough, I don't want to hear it, so take it back again.

220
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:00,990
Before I have you thrown in jail for marriage fraud.

221
00:16:01,990 --> 00:16:04,090
Take back what you just took back.

222
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:05,550
If you can change your mind once,

223
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:07,120
you can change it back again, can't you?

224
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:08,620
Change it back. I said change it back.

225
00:16:08,690 --> 00:16:11,720
Good grief, just change it back. Come on, change it back.

226
00:16:11,790 --> 00:16:13,020
I'm sorry.

227
00:16:14,050 --> 00:16:15,120
I really am.

228
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:18,020
I'm so sorry.

229
00:16:18,390 --> 00:16:20,320
Is sorry supposed to fix everything?

230
00:16:34,190 --> 00:16:35,190
One more.

231
00:16:57,090 --> 00:16:58,090
What's with you?

232
00:17:01,090 --> 00:17:02,090
What do you mean?

233
00:17:04,590 --> 00:17:05,620
Are you going easy on me?

234
00:17:06,790 --> 00:17:08,490
Going easy?

235
00:17:09,620 --> 00:17:11,120
What do you mean, going easy?

236
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:12,960
You return all the hard shots,

237
00:17:13,020 --> 00:17:14,590
but you purposely mess up the easy ones.

238
00:17:15,150 --> 00:17:18,320
It was so obvious that you were going easy on me.

239
00:17:18,650 --> 00:17:20,090
It's because I return all the hard shots.

240
00:17:20,150 --> 00:17:21,820
By the time the easy ones come, I'm drained.

241
00:17:22,490 --> 00:17:24,820
If I could play this well consistently, why would I be here?

242
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:26,460
I'd be at Wimbledon already.

243
00:17:26,650 --> 00:17:27,920
Who put you up to this?

244
00:17:28,790 --> 00:17:30,050
Did someone pay you to lose to me?

245
00:17:30,190 --> 00:17:31,920
Money? Why would I take money?

246
00:17:32,490 --> 00:17:34,190
Back in Wando, I'm the son of a rich family too.

247
00:17:37,190 --> 00:17:38,190
Hey.

248
00:17:39,190 --> 00:17:40,250
Did Chairman Jang ask you to do it?

249
00:17:43,890 --> 00:17:44,920
You know the FBI, right?

250
00:17:45,190 --> 00:17:46,920
Should I call them and suggest they recruit you?

251
00:17:48,750 --> 00:17:51,050
Why would he ask a favor like that from you?

252
00:17:51,290 --> 00:17:52,650
Why do you think?

253
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:56,290
You're Mrs. Go's favorite punching bag these days.

254
00:17:56,790 --> 00:17:57,790
If I were the Chairman,

255
00:17:57,850 --> 00:17:59,390
I'd be walking on eggshells around you too.

256
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:05,790
What? You want to stop?

257
00:18:06,690 --> 00:18:08,750
What's the point? If we keep playing, I'll keep winning.

258
00:18:09,990 --> 00:18:10,990
Oh, man...

259
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,250
It's tough, my friend.

260
00:18:14,650 --> 00:18:18,020
One minute, she's yelling at you for making Seo Hyun cry,

261
00:18:18,150 --> 00:18:21,020
and when you agree to date her, she yells at you for that too.

262
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:23,050
What on earth does she want you to do?

263
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:24,890
It's like she's just toying with you.

264
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,350
She really needs to get her story straight.

265
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:28,820
But...

266
00:18:31,550 --> 00:18:33,990
If Seo Hyun ran away, would you take her in?

267
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:37,190
- What are you talking about? - She already did.

268
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:39,220
She ran away to our place.

269
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:41,590
To be precise, into your arms.

270
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:55,460
Mu Jin.

271
00:18:58,250 --> 00:18:59,390
What are you doing here?

272
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,790
I was hungry, so I'm having some cereal.

273
00:19:03,150 --> 00:19:04,920
Jung Woo gave me the code.

274
00:19:05,390 --> 00:19:06,790
Did you tell your parents you were leaving?

275
00:19:08,350 --> 00:19:11,420
No, I snuck out while my mom was at the salon.

276
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:14,150
I just texted her, so she probably knows by now.

277
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:18,620
- Let's go. - Go where?

278
00:19:19,050 --> 00:19:20,050
To your house.

279
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:24,120
Do you think I'm joking?

280
00:19:25,350 --> 00:19:27,420
I thought about it a thousand times, and I couldn't take it anymore.

281
00:19:27,550 --> 00:19:29,420
I ran away because I felt like I was going to die.

282
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:32,050
Your mother said she'd disown you if you kept seeing me.

283
00:19:32,850 --> 00:19:35,490
If Mom keeps being stubborn, then I'll disown her too.

284
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:37,990
If Dad keeps objecting, I'll disown him too.

285
00:19:38,290 --> 00:19:39,960
I can just cut ties with my parents. It's that simple.

286
00:19:42,390 --> 00:19:43,490
Don't be ridiculous.

287
00:19:43,750 --> 00:19:45,650
- Come with me. - Hey.

288
00:19:46,750 --> 00:19:48,320
Hey.

289
00:19:49,750 --> 00:19:51,050
I'm not going home.

290
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:53,890
If it makes you uncomfortable for me to stay at your place,

291
00:19:53,890 --> 00:19:55,150
then drop me off at a hotel.

292
00:19:57,790 --> 00:19:59,590
I'm not going home.

293
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:03,020
One person who cut all family ties and left home...

294
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:04,790
is enough. That can be me.

295
00:20:08,390 --> 00:20:10,150
Nothing will be solved this way.

296
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:13,150
What choice do I have?

297
00:20:13,590 --> 00:20:17,190
What if Mom objects to the very end? What if she keeps saying no?

298
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:19,150
Are you going to break up with me then?

299
00:20:19,620 --> 00:20:21,390
I'm going to try everything I can.

300
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:23,020
But what if we try everything we can,

301
00:20:23,090 --> 00:20:24,550
and she still says no?

302
00:20:24,550 --> 00:20:26,520
After we've tried everything we can,

303
00:20:27,390 --> 00:20:29,090
and there are no options left,

304
00:20:30,190 --> 00:20:31,290
we'll talk about it then.

305
00:20:40,190 --> 00:20:42,750
If you were going to be dragged back home so pathetically,

306
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:44,390
why did you bother leaving in the first place?

307
00:20:45,220 --> 00:20:47,290
I didn't exactly want to come back.

308
00:20:48,250 --> 00:20:49,250
What?

309
00:20:50,490 --> 00:20:51,490
I'm sorry.

310
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:54,850
If you keep opposing me and trying to...

311
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,050
stop me from seeing Mu Jin,

312
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:57,820
I'll really leave for good next time.

313
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,490
You might as well just disown me.

314
00:21:01,520 --> 00:21:03,650
How did my daughter turn out like this?

315
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:06,920
Mu Jin, have you spoiled my Seo Hyun?

316
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:10,920
Am I a child? Stop being so unreasonable, Mom.

317
00:21:12,150 --> 00:21:14,550
Please don't worry. If Seo Hyun leaves home,

318
00:21:14,620 --> 00:21:16,420
I'll bring her right back.

319
00:21:16,850 --> 00:21:17,890
Mu Jin.

320
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:22,990
When you act like this, you're making it impossible for me.

321
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:25,390
I keep losing my chances.

322
00:21:26,590 --> 00:21:28,720
It's because I feel bad for you.

323
00:21:28,850 --> 00:21:30,920
My mom shouldn't be treating you like this,

324
00:21:30,990 --> 00:21:32,790
and it's driving me crazy.

325
00:21:32,850 --> 00:21:35,490
I'm fine. Okay? I'm totally fine.

326
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:38,720
It's fine. You can say whatever you want to me.

327
00:21:39,050 --> 00:21:41,050
Ma'am, I understand how you feel.

328
00:21:41,120 --> 00:21:42,960
What is there to understand?

329
00:21:43,220 --> 00:21:45,090
My mom is the one being ridiculous.

330
00:21:45,150 --> 00:21:46,520
All my friends say she's being ridiculous.

331
00:21:46,590 --> 00:21:48,890
No one I know can understand it.

332
00:21:48,950 --> 00:21:50,290
Jang Seo Hyun.

333
00:21:50,690 --> 00:21:53,190
I know you must be disappointed, but I'll try harder.

334
00:21:53,820 --> 00:21:55,320
I know you really don't approve of me,

335
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:57,050
but I'll work that much harder.

336
00:21:59,050 --> 00:22:00,220
Say something.

337
00:22:00,220 --> 00:22:02,790
Why should someone as great as him have to take this?

338
00:22:02,850 --> 00:22:04,490
This is completely over the top, Mom.

339
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,120
Mom.

340
00:22:16,420 --> 00:22:19,390
(Suragan Side Dishes)

341
00:22:28,950 --> 00:22:30,320
(Now Hiring)

342
00:22:30,390 --> 00:22:31,790
(Honest applicants preferred)

343
00:22:33,490 --> 00:22:34,490
So,

344
00:22:34,990 --> 00:22:37,220
you should go look somewhere else. Okay?

345
00:22:38,450 --> 00:22:40,550
Why? Don't you get it?

346
00:22:41,190 --> 00:22:43,150
You're fired.

347
00:22:43,220 --> 00:22:44,720
You don't have a job now.

348
00:22:45,350 --> 00:22:47,220
One more thing.

349
00:22:47,290 --> 00:22:50,750
That house where your family lives now.

350
00:22:50,820 --> 00:22:54,020
You have to move out of there within three months, got it?

351
00:22:54,820 --> 00:22:58,920
- What? - I want to kick you out right now,

352
00:22:59,450 --> 00:23:02,090
but what is it? Tenant? Landlord?

353
00:23:02,150 --> 00:23:04,850
There's some thingamajig about that.

354
00:23:05,090 --> 00:23:08,450
It says you have to give at least three months' notice.

355
00:23:10,390 --> 00:23:11,390
The landlord of my house...

356
00:23:11,690 --> 00:23:15,590
said the house was haunted to keep people away.

357
00:23:15,650 --> 00:23:16,650
That's me.

358
00:23:17,350 --> 00:23:20,550
I'm the owner of that house. Understand?

359
00:23:20,990 --> 00:23:23,020
Your situation was so pitiful...

360
00:23:23,090 --> 00:23:26,320
that I even lied about the house being haunted,

361
00:23:26,420 --> 00:23:29,120
and rented it to you for practically no deposit or rent.

362
00:23:29,190 --> 00:23:30,450
That was me.

363
00:23:30,890 --> 00:23:35,020
I didn't know you'd stab me in the back like this.

364
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:39,550
Now that you know I'm a wealthy woman with several properties.

365
00:23:39,550 --> 00:23:40,590
So what?

366
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:44,190
Do you want to reconsider?

367
00:23:44,820 --> 00:23:47,150
If you apologize right now,

368
00:23:47,890 --> 00:23:51,250
I might give you one more chance.

369
00:23:56,250 --> 00:23:58,350
I'm sorry.

370
00:23:59,750 --> 00:24:00,790
Oh, for heaven's sake.

371
00:24:01,850 --> 00:24:04,220
Look at her, throwing away her own good fortune.

372
00:24:05,690 --> 00:24:09,220
All right, then. You're out of a home and a job,

373
00:24:09,290 --> 00:24:12,320
so let's just go our separate ways, shall we?

374
00:24:26,720 --> 00:24:29,050
(Suragan Side Dishes)

375
00:24:35,190 --> 00:24:36,490
(Naeil Bank)

376
00:24:36,550 --> 00:24:38,490
(5,014 dollars)

377
00:24:49,490 --> 00:24:50,590
Gyu Young.

378
00:24:50,950 --> 00:24:52,920
I'm so sorry to ask,

379
00:24:53,020 --> 00:24:54,650
but we have to move out,

380
00:24:54,650 --> 00:24:56,920
so I need some money for a deposit.

381
00:24:58,390 --> 00:24:59,920
(Gyu Young)

382
00:24:59,990 --> 00:25:01,450
The first one is around 20,000 dollars,

383
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:03,250
and the other is closer to 25,000 dollars.

384
00:25:03,420 --> 00:25:04,920
Which one should I get, honey?

385
00:25:10,290 --> 00:25:11,820
Sorry. Wrong person.

386
00:25:20,650 --> 00:25:21,650
What?

387
00:25:22,250 --> 00:25:23,550
That's not 20 dollars, is it?

388
00:25:24,050 --> 00:25:26,820
Are you buying your fiancé a 20,000-dollar watch?

389
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:30,020
What's it to you? I told you I sent it by mistake.

390
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:31,220
But with our finances...

391
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:36,220
How can you afford this?

392
00:25:37,020 --> 00:25:38,750
Our stepdad gave me a ton of wedding money.

393
00:25:38,750 --> 00:25:40,290
I'm using that. Why?

394
00:25:41,850 --> 00:25:44,350
Surprising, isn't it? The wealth gap is just wild.

395
00:25:44,590 --> 00:25:46,320
That's the world Mom lives in.

396
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:48,550
It's the world I'm going to live in from now on.

397
00:25:49,550 --> 00:25:54,120
That's why Mom never came to see us or even pretended to know us.

398
00:25:54,190 --> 00:25:55,350
She was afraid we'd be a liability...

399
00:25:55,420 --> 00:25:56,890
and she'd get thrown out of her new world.

400
00:25:57,220 --> 00:25:59,290
She was afraid we'd cling to her like leeches.

401
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:02,320
So once I'm married, you pretend you don't know me either.

402
00:26:02,550 --> 00:26:04,650
You know how much I hate bugs, right?

403
00:26:04,990 --> 00:26:06,150
Especially parasites.

404
00:26:10,790 --> 00:26:12,850
Darn it. This is so frustrating.

405
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:16,750
(My Love)

406
00:26:17,890 --> 00:26:19,350
The first one is around 20,000 dollars,

407
00:26:19,420 --> 00:26:20,990
and the other is closer to 25,000 dollars.

408
00:26:21,050 --> 00:26:22,690
Which one should I get, honey?

409
00:26:29,450 --> 00:26:30,450
Honey.

410
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:32,720
Are you struggling financially these days?

411
00:26:33,550 --> 00:26:34,590
What?

412
00:26:36,590 --> 00:26:38,190
You can't be serious.

413
00:26:38,250 --> 00:26:40,820
Were you thinking of this as my daily watch?

414
00:26:43,890 --> 00:26:45,320
I thought I made myself perfectly clear...

415
00:26:45,390 --> 00:26:47,620
about the brand and model I want.

416
00:26:49,490 --> 00:26:50,890
No, it's just...

417
00:26:50,950 --> 00:26:52,320
I thought since your wedding watch is...

418
00:26:52,390 --> 00:26:54,850
- already high-end... - High-end?

419
00:26:56,050 --> 00:26:59,450
Hey. Since you brought it up,

420
00:27:00,620 --> 00:27:03,450
did you know my friends are asking if you're scamming me?

421
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:05,850
They're telling me I should run a proper background check on you.

422
00:27:06,420 --> 00:27:07,420
Scamming you?

423
00:27:07,790 --> 00:27:09,620
- A background check? - Yes.

424
00:27:09,990 --> 00:27:11,890
Your taste in wedding gifts says a lot...

425
00:27:11,950 --> 00:27:13,620
about your family and background.

426
00:27:14,220 --> 00:27:15,520
And as for your class...

427
00:27:20,250 --> 00:27:22,920
they think you're a mom-and-pop shop owner's daughter.

428
00:27:22,920 --> 00:27:24,490
Are you done talking?

429
00:27:24,850 --> 00:27:26,050
No, I'm not.

430
00:27:26,650 --> 00:27:29,250
There's a lot more I want to say, but I'm holding back.

431
00:27:30,790 --> 00:27:32,050
Out of respect for your pride.

432
00:27:33,990 --> 00:27:36,820
So what's your point? Do you want to call off the wedding?

433
00:27:37,290 --> 00:27:38,320
Do you want to?

434
00:27:40,650 --> 00:27:42,390
If you want to call it off, then go ahead.

435
00:27:44,550 --> 00:27:46,750
Why are you doing this to me? Did something happen?

436
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:48,920
Why are you suddenly acting this way?

437
00:28:01,390 --> 00:28:02,750
You know my friend Chang Woo, right?

438
00:28:05,220 --> 00:28:07,490
He said his mother-in-law bought him a new car the other day.

439
00:28:07,750 --> 00:28:11,390
And Dong Young's father-in-law got him a golf club membership.

440
00:28:18,420 --> 00:28:20,450
Then they ask me, "Sung Wook, what did your in-laws get you?"

441
00:28:20,520 --> 00:28:22,620
And I have nothing to say.

442
00:28:25,390 --> 00:28:26,590
What do you mean you have nothing to say?

443
00:28:26,850 --> 00:28:28,350
Just say you got some spending money.

444
00:28:29,250 --> 00:28:31,620
How much? A thousand dollars?

445
00:28:32,250 --> 00:28:33,520
To buy myself some gum?

446
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:35,750
A hundred thousand.

447
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:41,250
I already feel pathetic enough, do you have to lie about it too?

448
00:28:41,420 --> 00:28:42,550
I'm not lying.

449
00:28:51,850 --> 00:28:55,390
My dad told me to give this to you, but I completely forgot.

450
00:29:07,220 --> 00:29:08,620
(Cashier's Check, One Hundred Thousand Dollars)

451
00:29:10,550 --> 00:29:12,420
Oh, honey. Your father shouldn't have...

452
00:29:13,290 --> 00:29:16,190
So, do I still seem like a mom-and-pop shop owner's daughter?

453
00:29:17,050 --> 00:29:18,050
No.

454
00:29:19,620 --> 00:29:21,050
You're department store-level.

455
00:29:21,390 --> 00:29:23,520
On par with a seven-star hotel.

456
00:29:23,650 --> 00:29:26,690
No, I was just saying what some ignorant fools said.

457
00:29:26,690 --> 00:29:30,050
Me? I've always known your true worth.

458
00:29:31,320 --> 00:29:32,790
- Honey. - Yes?

459
00:29:33,220 --> 00:29:35,120
- Just... - Go on.

460
00:29:35,420 --> 00:29:36,550
go get me a caffè latte.

461
00:29:37,820 --> 00:29:39,920
I'll be right back with it.

462
00:29:42,150 --> 00:29:43,150
And the watch...

463
00:29:43,920 --> 00:29:45,850
Let's just get that one from earlier. Keep it simple.

464
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:48,020
You want to get a watch too?

465
00:29:48,420 --> 00:29:50,020
You said you'd buy me one.

466
00:29:51,950 --> 00:29:52,950
That's right.

467
00:29:55,020 --> 00:29:56,220
And no syrup for me.

468
00:29:56,990 --> 00:29:58,020
Okay.

469
00:29:59,250 --> 00:30:01,750
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

470
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:03,990
Did you meet up with Kwon Hee Na?

471
00:30:05,690 --> 00:30:06,690
Did she not show up?

472
00:30:07,220 --> 00:30:08,390
How late did you wait?

473
00:30:09,150 --> 00:30:10,150
Until dawn.

474
00:30:11,020 --> 00:30:12,850
Min Ju said she definitely gave her the message.

475
00:30:13,590 --> 00:30:14,590
Maybe she was busy?

476
00:30:15,090 --> 00:30:16,250
I guess she just didn't want to come.

477
00:30:16,990 --> 00:30:18,790
Hey, what kind of girl would dare turn you down?

478
00:30:21,550 --> 00:30:22,550
Oh, right.

479
00:30:22,620 --> 00:30:24,920
Min Ju said she's meeting with Hee Na again today.

480
00:30:26,520 --> 00:30:27,850
I know where they're meeting.

481
00:30:28,290 --> 00:30:30,290
Want to just "accidentally" run into them?

482
00:30:31,820 --> 00:30:34,590
Hey, if she won't come to you, a man has to go to her.

483
00:30:35,420 --> 00:30:37,220
Forget it. I don't want to scare her.

484
00:30:37,990 --> 00:30:39,550
After you've missed her for all these years,

485
00:30:39,820 --> 00:30:42,290
you're just going to let her go? You're the one and only Han Gyu Oh.

486
00:30:43,950 --> 00:30:46,090
Hey, come on. Let's go.

487
00:30:46,250 --> 00:30:47,920
Let's go get Kwon Hee Na.

488
00:30:50,090 --> 00:30:51,090
Sit down.

489
00:30:53,090 --> 00:30:54,090
You want me to sit down?

490
00:30:55,350 --> 00:30:57,490
But we're not that close, are we?

491
00:31:00,750 --> 00:31:01,750
So what?

492
00:31:02,550 --> 00:31:04,190
Then why are you trying so hard to help me?

493
00:31:04,590 --> 00:31:06,090
You helped me out before.

494
00:31:06,950 --> 00:31:07,950
I did?

495
00:31:07,950 --> 00:31:09,490
I was getting beat up by some bullies...

496
00:31:09,550 --> 00:31:11,090
and they were about to take my money,

497
00:31:11,920 --> 00:31:13,050
but you saved me.

498
00:31:17,390 --> 00:31:18,390
I don't remember that.

499
00:31:19,650 --> 00:31:21,450
Well, it's not like I was the only kid...

500
00:31:21,520 --> 00:31:22,520
you helped back then.

501
00:31:23,290 --> 00:31:25,390
You were so cool back then.

502
00:31:26,220 --> 00:31:27,890
You were a total superman.

503
00:31:28,390 --> 00:31:30,850
That's enough. It's so cringey. Let's stop.

504
00:31:34,320 --> 00:31:36,790
Are you really not going to give it another shot with Kwon Hee Na?

505
00:31:37,020 --> 00:31:38,120
Are you done eating?

506
00:31:40,290 --> 00:31:41,790
Hey, what do you do for work anyway?

507
00:31:42,120 --> 00:31:44,590
I asked Yoon Gi, but he said he didn't really know either.

508
00:31:58,920 --> 00:32:00,920
- It's obvious. - Totally.

509
00:32:00,990 --> 00:32:02,390
- A gigolo. - A gigolo.

510
00:32:05,690 --> 00:32:07,690
From your voice, you sound like a kid.

511
00:32:07,690 --> 00:32:08,750
I don't do kids.

512
00:32:08,890 --> 00:32:11,620
- Call me when you're older. - Wow, what a lowlife...

513
00:32:12,790 --> 00:32:14,690
Does your mom know you live like this?

514
00:32:15,450 --> 00:32:17,520
That her son seduces women her age...

515
00:32:17,520 --> 00:32:19,790
and lives like a parasite? Does she know?

516
00:32:24,190 --> 00:32:26,020
What did the rice cakes ever do to you?

517
00:32:29,090 --> 00:32:30,520
It's too spicy.

518
00:32:31,620 --> 00:32:33,650
You're the one who ordered level three 'super spicy'.

519
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:36,590
Right, so I ordered level three, but why isn't it spicy at all?

520
00:32:38,650 --> 00:32:40,150
Who did this to you?

521
00:32:41,290 --> 00:32:43,250
What happened when you met Han Gyu Oh?

522
00:32:46,690 --> 00:32:47,690
I didn't meet him.

523
00:32:48,920 --> 00:32:49,920
You didn't?

524
00:32:51,990 --> 00:32:54,390
Well, it's not like I have to meet him.

525
00:32:55,650 --> 00:32:57,920
Right. I mean, you don't have to, but...

526
00:32:59,450 --> 00:33:00,450
Aren't you interested?

527
00:33:01,290 --> 00:33:02,390
You're never going to see him?

528
00:33:03,590 --> 00:33:04,690
Right.

529
00:33:42,920 --> 00:33:46,190
That phone number for that Gigolo from before.

530
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:49,020
Do you still have it?

531
00:33:49,850 --> 00:33:52,250
No, I deleted it right after that whole thing with my mom.

532
00:33:52,320 --> 00:33:53,320
He was disgusting.

533
00:33:55,020 --> 00:33:56,390
Why do you want that Gigolo's number?

534
00:33:57,520 --> 00:33:58,520
What?

535
00:34:00,020 --> 00:34:01,020
It's just...

536
00:34:01,590 --> 00:34:05,150
Do you think maybe that number was wrong?

537
00:34:06,090 --> 00:34:09,320
- What? - Besides 010, of the eight digits,

538
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:11,950
maybe one of them was wrong.

539
00:34:12,520 --> 00:34:14,720
I mean, we were drinking then.

540
00:34:15,890 --> 00:34:20,020
I feel like maybe I misdialed one digit.

541
00:34:21,150 --> 00:34:23,790
Then they would've said, "I think you have the wrong number."

542
00:34:24,250 --> 00:34:25,920
You were going back and forth with him, saying nasty words.

543
00:34:25,990 --> 00:34:27,190
You really got into it with him.

544
00:34:29,290 --> 00:34:30,990
Is level three the spiciest they have here?

545
00:34:31,050 --> 00:34:32,050
Don't they have anything spicier?

546
00:34:33,790 --> 00:34:35,720
You're acting really weird today.

547
00:34:36,450 --> 00:34:38,150
There's no flow to this conversation,

548
00:34:38,220 --> 00:34:39,490
and no rhyme or reason to it.

549
00:34:42,390 --> 00:34:43,390
But, Kwon Hee Na.

550
00:34:44,890 --> 00:34:47,590
Are you really never going to see Han Gyu Oh again?

551
00:34:48,050 --> 00:34:49,590
Like, for real? The end?

552
00:34:50,090 --> 00:34:52,290
Don't you ever mention Han Gyu Oh in front of me again.

553
00:34:53,250 --> 00:34:55,620
Ma'am, can we get more spicy sauce over here?

554
00:34:56,190 --> 00:34:58,450
Okay, then I'll just say one last thing about Han Gyu Oh.

555
00:34:59,590 --> 00:35:01,250
Let me have Han Gyu Oh.

556
00:35:03,490 --> 00:35:04,860
You said you weren't going to see him, right?

557
00:35:05,320 --> 00:35:06,320
So I'll see him instead.

558
00:35:06,750 --> 00:35:07,750
Hey.

559
00:35:09,390 --> 00:35:11,550
Hey, you have a boyfriend.

560
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:14,420
And your boyfriend is Han Gyu Oh's friend.

561
00:35:14,520 --> 00:35:15,520
Right.

562
00:35:16,050 --> 00:35:18,590
But when Han Gyu Oh and Su Chan were sitting next to each other,

563
00:35:18,650 --> 00:35:21,420
Han Gyu Oh is radiating this incredible aura,

564
00:35:21,690 --> 00:35:24,150
and my Su Chan ends up looking like a nobody.

565
00:35:24,520 --> 00:35:25,790
What do you think of that?

566
00:35:26,420 --> 00:35:28,790
No, hey, you can't say that.

567
00:35:29,820 --> 00:35:32,020
I don't care what you say.

568
00:35:32,450 --> 00:35:33,890
I'm planning to break up with Su Chan soon anyway.

569
00:35:34,420 --> 00:35:35,420
No.

570
00:35:35,720 --> 00:35:37,550
He can date anyone but you.

571
00:35:38,650 --> 00:35:41,120
Why not? You said you don't like Han Gyu Oh.

572
00:35:43,150 --> 00:35:44,420
Either way, absolutely not.

573
00:35:44,550 --> 00:35:46,620
I don't care if you break up with your boyfriend,

574
00:35:46,690 --> 00:35:48,750
and I don't care who else you fall for,

575
00:35:49,550 --> 00:35:50,920
but you can have any other man in the world,

576
00:35:50,990 --> 00:35:52,020
but absolutely not Han Gyu Oh.

577
00:35:55,620 --> 00:35:58,250
But why am I even asking for your permission?

578
00:35:59,290 --> 00:36:01,690
You're not his mother or his girlfriend.

579
00:36:01,990 --> 00:36:03,860
It's not like you own him.

580
00:36:04,290 --> 00:36:05,650
Min Ju.

581
00:36:06,420 --> 00:36:08,920
I probably won't be contacting you anymore,

582
00:36:09,120 --> 00:36:10,420
but if you call me, I'll answer.

583
00:36:12,150 --> 00:36:13,150
Contact me.

584
00:36:44,750 --> 00:36:45,750
Hello.

585
00:36:46,420 --> 00:36:47,950
I heard you're not taking jobs for a while.

586
00:36:49,890 --> 00:36:50,890
That's right.

587
00:36:51,120 --> 00:36:52,590
Did you land a big spender or something?

588
00:36:54,420 --> 00:36:55,520
It's not like that.

589
00:36:56,360 --> 00:36:57,420
I'm in the middle of something urgent,

590
00:36:57,490 --> 00:36:58,490
so I'll call you back...

591
00:36:58,550 --> 00:37:00,090
When are you going to pay off your debt...

592
00:37:00,150 --> 00:37:01,290
if you're so picky about jobs?

593
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:03,620
Don't you know interest keeps piling up...

594
00:37:03,690 --> 00:37:04,720
while you're messing around?

595
00:37:05,390 --> 00:37:07,220
How long do you think you're going to be popular?

596
00:37:07,920 --> 00:37:09,250
You'll be 30 before you know it,

597
00:37:09,420 --> 00:37:10,950
and the guys in their 20s will take your place.

598
00:37:11,490 --> 00:37:12,490
It happens in a flash.

599
00:37:13,050 --> 00:37:15,620
- Make money while you can. - I'm sorry.

600
00:37:16,020 --> 00:37:18,320
- I'm hanging up now. - Hey, you bastard.

601
00:37:19,220 --> 00:37:21,290
Why are you getting involved in someone else's problems?

602
00:37:21,690 --> 00:37:22,750
Even if you work until you die,

603
00:37:22,820 --> 00:37:24,150
do you think you can ever pay off that debt?

604
00:37:35,750 --> 00:37:36,750
Look at him.

605
00:37:46,290 --> 00:37:47,290
Darn.

606
00:37:49,590 --> 00:37:51,390
Hey, get him.

607
00:38:21,090 --> 00:38:22,090
Darn it.

608
00:38:26,620 --> 00:38:29,650
Hey, you bastard, where do you think you're going?

609
00:39:01,620 --> 00:39:03,390
(Sehyeon General Hospital Main Building)

610
00:39:06,190 --> 00:39:07,190
For the rest of my life,

611
00:39:07,650 --> 00:39:09,050
I will take care of you.

612
00:39:10,250 --> 00:39:11,750
Until I can put you back the way you were.

613
00:39:30,790 --> 00:39:32,050
Ma'am.

614
00:39:32,390 --> 00:39:35,050
You currently have an outstanding loan.

615
00:39:35,290 --> 00:39:37,520
We've also confirmed a history of some late payments.

616
00:39:39,450 --> 00:39:42,050
Then how much more would be possible?

617
00:39:54,050 --> 00:39:55,250
It's about Gyu Rim and me.

618
00:39:56,920 --> 00:39:58,390
We're going back to being friends.

619
00:39:58,920 --> 00:40:00,920
We decided to go back to how we used to be.

620
00:40:04,890 --> 00:40:05,890
And?

621
00:40:06,550 --> 00:40:08,450
You don't seem very happy about that.

622
00:40:09,590 --> 00:40:10,690
Am I supposed to be happy?

623
00:40:12,020 --> 00:40:15,990
I guess it's really over between you and Gyu Rim.

624
00:40:16,860 --> 00:40:17,860
Look.

625
00:40:18,920 --> 00:40:20,990
Sitting here face-to-face with you right now...

626
00:40:21,750 --> 00:40:23,360
is making me extremely uncomfortable.

627
00:40:25,860 --> 00:40:27,050
So you're saying I should say...

628
00:40:27,050 --> 00:40:28,490
what I came to say and then get lost.

629
00:40:28,550 --> 00:40:29,550
Is that it?

630
00:40:30,820 --> 00:40:31,820
Right.

631
00:40:32,020 --> 00:40:33,520
Then I'll make it quick and get out of here.

632
00:40:36,990 --> 00:40:38,050
Gyu Rim said...

633
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:41,990
that she didn't want to lie to herself or me anymore...

634
00:40:42,950 --> 00:40:45,190
and that we should pretend the proposal never happened.

635
00:40:45,820 --> 00:40:48,090
I said, "Okay, let's do that."

636
00:40:48,550 --> 00:40:50,360
I also said that it was really awkward for me too.

637
00:40:51,220 --> 00:40:53,150
and that we should see each other at our monthly get-together.

638
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:55,090
And then I went home.

639
00:40:59,250 --> 00:41:02,590
I made some fried eggs, and mixed them with some rice.

640
00:41:04,550 --> 00:41:06,450
I honestly thought I'd be okay.

641
00:41:08,490 --> 00:41:10,720
But as time went on,

642
00:41:11,150 --> 00:41:15,150
it felt like there was a gaping hole in my chest.

643
00:41:16,690 --> 00:41:19,720
I couldn't get a grip and I just felt lost.

644
00:41:21,290 --> 00:41:23,150
I mean, it felt like my world had ended.

645
00:41:24,590 --> 00:41:26,250
I couldn't bring myself to sit down.

646
00:41:26,750 --> 00:41:28,290
I couldn't even stand up.

647
00:41:29,820 --> 00:41:31,890
I thought about going to see a psychiatrist,

648
00:41:32,320 --> 00:41:34,390
but before I knew it, I was heading toward you, Chef.

649
00:41:34,790 --> 00:41:36,250
My feet just brought me here.

650
00:41:42,790 --> 00:41:44,020
Do I look like a pushover to you?

651
00:41:44,220 --> 00:41:45,220
No.

652
00:41:45,620 --> 00:41:48,550
Chef, you were dumped by Gyu Rim before I was, weren't you?

653
00:41:49,290 --> 00:41:52,420
I feel this awful, and I never even got to hold her hand.

654
00:41:52,590 --> 00:41:54,690
But you had such a passionate romance with her.

655
00:41:54,950 --> 00:41:56,920
How did you endure the pain of that ordeal?

656
00:41:57,050 --> 00:41:58,650
Can't you give me some advice?

657
00:42:00,220 --> 00:42:03,390
I mean, anything. Some know-how for getting over it,

658
00:42:03,650 --> 00:42:05,650
or even if you can't get over it,

659
00:42:05,750 --> 00:42:07,820
something to do to make it hurt a little less.

660
00:42:08,050 --> 00:42:09,790
Or something to make the time pass faster.

661
00:42:09,790 --> 00:42:11,520
Any kind of tip, please.

662
00:42:12,550 --> 00:42:13,550
I'll get you a taxi.

663
00:42:15,650 --> 00:42:17,220
I know how to get a taxi.

664
00:42:18,250 --> 00:42:19,790
Please, just tell me.

665
00:42:20,090 --> 00:42:22,250
How can I be okay like you are?

666
00:42:23,050 --> 00:42:25,650
When will it finally stop hurting?

667
00:42:27,290 --> 00:42:29,290
Park Jung Woo.

668
00:42:29,690 --> 00:42:30,890
What?

669
00:42:34,890 --> 00:42:36,390
Show this gentleman the way out...

670
00:42:36,620 --> 00:42:37,620
and call him a taxi.

671
00:42:38,150 --> 00:42:40,250
I told you I can get my own taxi.

672
00:42:41,390 --> 00:42:44,390
I think he needs an ambulance, not a taxi.

673
00:42:50,150 --> 00:42:51,860
I know I'm not acting normal,

674
00:42:53,360 --> 00:42:54,550
but I'm not crazy.

675
00:42:55,890 --> 00:42:58,050
I was just so desperate that...

676
00:43:01,360 --> 00:43:02,360
Never mind.

677
00:43:03,120 --> 00:43:04,720
I am crazy.

678
00:43:05,890 --> 00:43:07,690
If I ever show up here again,

679
00:43:08,360 --> 00:43:10,320
just throw salt on me.

680
00:43:19,520 --> 00:43:23,090
(Danim-Gil Knife-Cut Noodles)

681
00:43:30,620 --> 00:43:32,520
What are you staring at?

682
00:43:33,450 --> 00:43:34,450
Hello, ma'am.

683
00:43:37,390 --> 00:43:38,390
What is this?

684
00:43:40,250 --> 00:43:42,020
It's a flyer for a new tuna restaurant.

685
00:43:44,520 --> 00:43:45,820
Are you craving some tuna?

686
00:43:46,020 --> 00:43:49,290
My one wish is to eat tuna until I burst, before I die

687
00:43:50,450 --> 00:43:51,850
Well, if you like it that much,

688
00:43:52,450 --> 00:43:54,820
you should go get some instead of just standing here.

689
00:43:55,020 --> 00:43:58,390
Thirty dollars for all-you-can-eat isn't a bad price.

690
00:43:58,450 --> 00:44:00,190
They even have a ten percent discount for the grand opening.

691
00:44:01,450 --> 00:44:02,950
Not the all-you-can-eat kind.

692
00:44:03,120 --> 00:44:04,390
The kind that costs over 100 dollars a person.

693
00:44:04,520 --> 00:44:06,920
Tuna omakase. And when it comes to tuna,

694
00:44:07,420 --> 00:44:09,920
I go crazy for the eyeball, the gills, and the belly meat...

695
00:44:10,320 --> 00:44:13,990
Come on, you idiot. Is this really the time for you...

696
00:44:14,050 --> 00:44:16,020
to be going on about tuna?

697
00:44:16,850 --> 00:44:17,950
Darn it.

698
00:44:18,950 --> 00:44:20,350
I'm so immature.

699
00:44:21,750 --> 00:44:23,190
I should stop being a burden on my children.

700
00:44:23,250 --> 00:44:26,120
I should've just killed myself a long time ago.

701
00:44:28,050 --> 00:44:30,390
Maybe I should just go to the Han River now?

702
00:44:30,990 --> 00:44:32,420
It's not the Han River's fault.

703
00:44:34,490 --> 00:44:36,920
You're right. The Han River is innocent.

704
00:44:37,790 --> 00:44:39,220
I'm the sinner here.

705
00:44:39,850 --> 00:44:41,720
In a dire situation like this,

706
00:44:41,820 --> 00:44:43,090
here I am, just thinking about tuna.

707
00:44:43,550 --> 00:44:47,190
But talking about tuna again, it's making my mouth water.

708
00:44:48,420 --> 00:44:50,590
Am I even human?

709
00:44:52,820 --> 00:44:56,350
- Do you want tuna that badly? - Yes.

710
00:44:56,650 --> 00:44:57,950
I mean, no.

711
00:44:58,920 --> 00:45:01,120
Okay, forget about it. Don't think about it.

712
00:45:01,120 --> 00:45:02,750
Don't think about it.

713
00:45:03,650 --> 00:45:04,650
The tuna.

714
00:45:06,150 --> 00:45:08,190
It's my treat. Let's go get some.

715
00:45:08,890 --> 00:45:13,390
Just to be clear, I was talking about tuna omakase.

716
00:45:13,490 --> 00:45:14,490
Follow me.

717
00:45:15,450 --> 00:45:18,050
Wait, did she mishear "tuna" as "mackerel"?

718
00:45:19,150 --> 00:45:21,920
It's not mackerel, it's tuna.

719
00:45:22,920 --> 00:45:25,650
Oh, she must have heard "mackerel" again.

720
00:45:26,220 --> 00:45:27,220
Come on.

721
00:45:32,490 --> 00:45:33,490
Help yourself.

722
00:45:33,550 --> 00:45:36,350
I'm not dreaming, am I?

723
00:45:37,350 --> 00:45:39,550
It's not a dream, so hurry up and eat.

724
00:45:39,890 --> 00:45:42,590
How much is this per person?

725
00:45:42,890 --> 00:45:44,190
Three hundred dollars.

726
00:45:44,690 --> 00:45:45,690
Three hundred?

727
00:45:47,250 --> 00:45:48,250
Enjoy your meal.

728
00:45:49,850 --> 00:45:53,490
They're going to serve the tuna eyeball separately in a drink,

729
00:45:53,620 --> 00:45:54,620
so go ahead and eat.

730
00:45:56,320 --> 00:45:57,790
Did you win the lottery?

731
00:45:59,190 --> 00:46:01,050
No, not the lottery,

732
00:46:01,990 --> 00:46:05,020
but I hit the jackpot today. So just relax and enjoy your meal.

733
00:46:08,120 --> 00:46:09,650
Why are you being so nice to me?

734
00:46:11,320 --> 00:46:12,320
Well,

735
00:46:12,850 --> 00:46:15,120
I owe you for helping me...

736
00:46:15,190 --> 00:46:16,520
when I was embarrassed by the couple with the fake shoes.

737
00:46:17,650 --> 00:46:20,590
And also because I feel a little sorry for you.

738
00:46:22,720 --> 00:46:24,550
Are you taking pity on me?

739
00:46:25,320 --> 00:46:27,190
Oh, it's not pity.

740
00:46:29,090 --> 00:46:30,350
It's okay if it's pity.

741
00:46:30,750 --> 00:46:31,920
Pity is a form of caring, after all.

742
00:46:32,550 --> 00:46:34,050
In this cruel world,

743
00:46:34,350 --> 00:46:35,950
we should live by sharing whatever kindness we can.

744
00:46:37,290 --> 00:46:38,920
And from now on, please don't speak formally.

745
00:46:39,490 --> 00:46:40,790
I'm younger, so you can call me "Seok Joong."

746
00:46:41,890 --> 00:46:42,890
Please, use my name.

747
00:46:43,390 --> 00:46:44,990
You can speak informally, too. Ma'am.

748
00:46:46,190 --> 00:46:47,190
One thing at a time.

749
00:46:47,450 --> 00:46:49,720
- Please, eat up. - Okay.

750
00:46:54,820 --> 00:46:56,290
What is it?

751
00:46:57,450 --> 00:46:58,490
What?

752
00:46:59,220 --> 00:47:02,050
Please, keep eating. I just have to take this call.

753
00:47:02,120 --> 00:47:04,650
Okay, ma'am...

754
00:47:13,320 --> 00:47:14,490
This is so delicious.

755
00:47:15,450 --> 00:47:16,690
(Grand Hall)

756
00:47:16,750 --> 00:47:17,750
Great work.

757
00:47:18,790 --> 00:47:19,820
Great work.

758
00:47:20,220 --> 00:47:22,420
- Gyu Seo. - Director.

759
00:47:22,550 --> 00:47:24,020
Weren't you nervous at all?

760
00:47:24,190 --> 00:47:25,390
I heard this was your first time on stage.

761
00:47:25,890 --> 00:47:28,350
- I was incredibly nervous. - You were?

762
00:47:28,350 --> 00:47:29,990
What? Why are you all still here?

763
00:47:30,050 --> 00:47:32,490
I got a text. The after-party is at the club downstairs.

764
00:47:32,550 --> 00:47:33,720
Didn't you get the message?

765
00:47:34,050 --> 00:47:35,050
What about you?

766
00:47:36,220 --> 00:47:38,390
- I think I'll skip it. - Hey, why not?

767
00:47:38,390 --> 00:47:41,650
- Come with us. - He's underage, you idiot.

768
00:47:42,020 --> 00:47:44,490
- Really? - You're going to get in trouble.

769
00:47:47,850 --> 00:47:52,150
You're so handsome. I mean, honey, why are you so good-looking?

770
00:47:53,120 --> 00:47:54,390
I thought you said you were quitting.

771
00:47:58,420 --> 00:48:00,590
Didn't you say you'd quit before Gyu Rim finds out?

772
00:48:02,620 --> 00:48:04,620
Sorry, but can you go on ahead?

773
00:48:05,090 --> 00:48:06,190
Why?

774
00:48:06,450 --> 00:48:07,450
Who's that?

775
00:48:08,490 --> 00:48:10,590
- Do you know him, honey? - Who are you calling him 'honey'?

776
00:48:11,150 --> 00:48:12,950
Why is my brother your honey, ma'am?

777
00:48:14,850 --> 00:48:15,850
Hey.

778
00:48:16,790 --> 00:48:17,890
I'll be right there.

779
00:48:18,020 --> 00:48:19,020
Just go on ahead.

780
00:48:26,520 --> 00:48:28,150
What on earth are you up to?

781
00:48:29,250 --> 00:48:31,120
Should I really tell Gyu Rim everything?

782
00:48:32,320 --> 00:48:33,320
Go.

783
00:48:34,150 --> 00:48:35,720
For today, let's just pretend you saw nothing.

784
00:48:39,920 --> 00:48:42,090
Trash like you can't even be recycled.

785
00:48:42,590 --> 00:48:43,590
Get it?

786
00:48:47,220 --> 00:48:48,220
I won't let you go.

787
00:48:52,520 --> 00:48:54,990
- Keep it up and you'll get punched. - Look who's talking.

788
00:48:55,890 --> 00:48:56,990
Just try and leave.

789
00:48:57,250 --> 00:49:00,290
- I will break both of your legs. - I'm counting to three.

790
00:49:00,390 --> 00:49:01,490
- One. - Two.

791
00:49:01,920 --> 00:49:02,950
Three.

792
00:49:04,190 --> 00:49:05,220
Hit me.

793
00:49:05,720 --> 00:49:06,720
Do it.

794
00:49:07,450 --> 00:49:08,450
I said, hit me.

795
00:49:09,620 --> 00:49:10,920
What's wrong? Can't you hit me?

796
00:49:11,120 --> 00:49:14,250
You have to throw the first punch so I can break your legs.

797
00:49:33,720 --> 00:49:36,350
Let go. I said, let go.

798
00:49:36,850 --> 00:49:40,950
(Geumje Police)

799
00:49:47,120 --> 00:49:49,450
(Geumje Police)

800
00:49:49,520 --> 00:49:51,320
(Major Crimes Team 1)

801
00:49:59,590 --> 00:50:02,490
I keep telling you, she is on her way.

802
00:50:03,290 --> 00:50:05,290
Why won't you believe me?

803
00:50:05,990 --> 00:50:06,990
Dad.

804
00:50:08,820 --> 00:50:09,820
Gyu Rim.

805
00:50:10,290 --> 00:50:14,790
Hey. How can people be so heartless?

806
00:50:19,020 --> 00:50:20,890
I'm Han Seok Joong's guardian.

807
00:50:21,850 --> 00:50:22,920
You heard what happened, right?

808
00:50:23,350 --> 00:50:25,120
Your father dined and dashed,

809
00:50:25,490 --> 00:50:28,250
- the restaurant filed a complaint. - Come on.

810
00:50:28,320 --> 00:50:30,190
I'm telling you, it wasn't a dine-and-dash.

811
00:50:30,650 --> 00:50:31,920
Some woman said she was buying me tuna.

812
00:50:31,990 --> 00:50:33,550
I just went along with her.

813
00:50:34,520 --> 00:50:35,690
If they had waited, she would have come.

814
00:50:35,750 --> 00:50:38,490
But the restaurant owner couldn't wait and reported me.

815
00:50:38,690 --> 00:50:40,190
They're the ones who are just plain rotten.

816
00:50:40,650 --> 00:50:42,250
You didn't have any money to pay for your meal?

817
00:50:43,020 --> 00:50:46,020
If you tell me which restaurant, I'll pay the bill.

818
00:50:46,390 --> 00:50:47,850
You can't afford it.

819
00:50:48,490 --> 00:50:51,620
If you tried to pay for that, you'd have a heart attack.

820
00:50:52,590 --> 00:50:54,350
How expensive was the place?

821
00:50:56,750 --> 00:50:58,120
It's 300 dollars a person.

822
00:50:59,620 --> 00:51:01,120
So that's 600 dollars for the two people.

823
00:51:01,320 --> 00:51:02,520
And that doesn't include the service charge.

824
00:51:03,190 --> 00:51:05,490
I'm telling you, the woman said she'd pay.

825
00:51:06,320 --> 00:51:09,190
Who did you eat with? Have you tried calling her?

826
00:51:10,720 --> 00:51:12,220
I don't know her phone number,

827
00:51:13,650 --> 00:51:14,790
her name,

828
00:51:15,350 --> 00:51:16,550
or her address.

829
00:51:17,590 --> 00:51:18,820
I don't know a single thing.

830
00:51:19,950 --> 00:51:22,450
You think she set me up and just took off?

831
00:51:27,520 --> 00:51:28,650
It's an unknown number.

832
00:51:28,650 --> 00:51:30,450
See? I told you she'd call.

833
00:51:32,250 --> 00:51:33,690
Ma'am, where...

834
00:51:36,150 --> 00:51:38,350
Where? The police station?

835
00:51:40,120 --> 00:51:43,220
Who are you, you bastard? Is this a phone scam?

836
00:51:43,890 --> 00:51:45,890
Don't give me that nonsense about a police station.

837
00:51:46,020 --> 00:51:48,520
I'm at the police station right now, you idiot.

838
00:51:52,220 --> 00:51:53,220
Han Gyu Seo?

839
00:51:55,150 --> 00:51:56,450
Han Gyu Seo is my son.

840
00:51:58,790 --> 00:51:59,820
Han Gyu Oh?

841
00:52:00,420 --> 00:52:01,750
Han Gyu Oh, too.

842
00:52:02,720 --> 00:52:04,290
He's also my son.

843
00:52:05,250 --> 00:52:07,690
Just one moment, sir.

844
00:52:09,650 --> 00:52:13,850
Gyu Oh and Gyu Seo got into a fight, and they're at the police station.

845
00:52:14,820 --> 00:52:16,650
Officer, what is all this about?

846
00:52:43,720 --> 00:52:45,920
(Gyu Young)

847
00:52:45,990 --> 00:52:46,990
(Gyu Young)

848
00:53:01,620 --> 00:53:02,620
One moment.

849
00:53:05,150 --> 00:53:06,450
Why is she calling?

850
00:53:06,950 --> 00:53:09,150
- Oh, no. - Han Gyu Young.

851
00:53:11,190 --> 00:53:12,190
Han Gyu Young.

852
00:53:13,650 --> 00:53:15,720
I'm swamped. Why do you keep calling?

853
00:53:15,990 --> 00:53:17,990
When someone keeps calling you,

854
00:53:18,920 --> 00:53:20,190
you should assume something big has happened...

855
00:53:20,250 --> 00:53:21,690
and call them back, don't you think?

856
00:53:22,050 --> 00:53:23,090
Important? Like what?

857
00:53:23,150 --> 00:53:24,450
Did the house burn down or something?

858
00:53:25,090 --> 00:53:27,020
I'm sending you the address. Get over here now.

859
00:53:27,450 --> 00:53:29,290
Come and pay for Dad's meal.

860
00:53:29,820 --> 00:53:30,950
What are you talking about?

861
00:53:31,190 --> 00:53:34,050
- Why should I pay for Dad's meal? - You said you have plenty of money.

862
00:53:34,220 --> 00:53:35,790
That's why your husband's watch cost tens of thousands...

863
00:53:38,320 --> 00:53:40,290
Anyway, come pay for Dad's meal...

864
00:53:40,350 --> 00:53:43,490
- and take him with you. - No way. You do it. I'm busy.

865
00:53:44,350 --> 00:53:46,990
I have to go see Gyu Oh and Gyu Seo right now.

866
00:53:49,220 --> 00:53:52,490
Then you pay the bill, take Dad, and go see Gyu Oh and Gyu Seo.

867
00:53:52,550 --> 00:53:53,550
I'm busy, so I'm hanging up.

868
00:53:53,620 --> 00:53:56,190
Why do I have to do everything myself?

869
00:53:56,520 --> 00:53:58,690
Hey, aren't you his daughter?

870
00:53:58,920 --> 00:54:00,790
Aren't you Gyu Oh and Gyu Seo's sister?

871
00:54:01,390 --> 00:54:02,790
What about you?

872
00:54:03,150 --> 00:54:05,450
Why do I always have to do everything by myself?

873
00:54:06,520 --> 00:54:08,720
Sacrificing yourself for the family...

874
00:54:08,890 --> 00:54:11,490
has always been your job as the dutiful eldest daughter, hasn't it?

875
00:54:11,890 --> 00:54:15,190
That's why Gyu Oh and the twins are so completely smitten with you.

876
00:54:15,450 --> 00:54:16,590
You got a taste for that,

877
00:54:16,590 --> 00:54:18,420
and you kept playing the good girl, didn't you?

878
00:54:18,850 --> 00:54:19,920
What did you say?

879
00:54:20,150 --> 00:54:21,990
Let's not get all dramatic.

880
00:54:22,050 --> 00:54:23,290
It's so unlike Cinderella.

881
00:54:28,950 --> 00:54:30,020
Darn it.

882
00:54:33,420 --> 00:54:34,620
I'll give you a big tip,

883
00:54:34,690 --> 00:54:35,820
so please pretend you didn't hear me.

884
00:54:35,950 --> 00:54:37,250
Yes, I understand.

885
00:54:40,550 --> 00:54:42,550
(Gangnam Police Station)

886
00:54:47,490 --> 00:54:49,950
(Seoul)

887
00:54:49,990 --> 00:54:51,720
We're here, ma'am.

888
00:54:54,090 --> 00:54:55,090
Ma'am.

889
00:54:57,090 --> 00:54:58,250
I'm sorry.

890
00:55:06,220 --> 00:55:08,420
Sir, I'm sorry.

891
00:55:08,690 --> 00:55:11,220
Could you drop me off at the nearest subway station?

892
00:55:11,650 --> 00:55:12,650
Sure.

893
00:55:17,450 --> 00:55:18,820
Are you out of your mind?

894
00:55:19,320 --> 00:55:20,520
How did you fight with Gyu Oh...

895
00:55:20,520 --> 00:55:21,790
that you ended up at the police station?

896
00:55:24,290 --> 00:55:25,290
Gyu Rim?

897
00:55:25,690 --> 00:55:27,220
I haven't heard anything from her.

898
00:55:27,650 --> 00:55:30,050
She told Dad she was coming to see Gyu Oh and me,

899
00:55:30,290 --> 00:55:31,320
but she's not here yet.

900
00:55:33,890 --> 00:55:35,090
And her phone is off.

901
00:55:36,550 --> 00:55:38,290
Dad came to the police station to pick us up.

902
00:55:38,650 --> 00:55:39,890
- It cannot be reached... - We were just released.

903
00:55:39,950 --> 00:55:41,150
We're on our way home now.

904
00:55:41,220 --> 00:55:42,850
You will be connected to the voice mailbox...

905
00:55:43,090 --> 00:55:44,550
Gyeol isn't answering his phone either.

906
00:55:44,950 --> 00:55:45,990
I'll call you back.

907
00:55:48,190 --> 00:55:50,520
- Where could Gyu Rim have gone? - The phone is turned off...

908
00:55:52,990 --> 00:55:54,520
Her phone is still off.

909
00:55:57,650 --> 00:55:59,990
Hey, why did you call her?

910
00:56:00,390 --> 00:56:01,650
Are you proud of getting into a fight?

911
00:56:01,990 --> 00:56:03,550
I didn't call Gyu Rim.

912
00:56:03,990 --> 00:56:06,590
I gave the police Dad's number so she wouldn't worry.

913
00:56:12,720 --> 00:56:15,520
Dad, why did you have to tell her?

914
00:56:16,520 --> 00:56:18,990
Gyu Rim has been to the police station many times,

915
00:56:19,450 --> 00:56:22,290
so I thought she might have some know-how.

916
00:56:24,390 --> 00:56:26,950
Hey, I sat in front of a cop for three hours earlier,

917
00:56:27,120 --> 00:56:28,220
and I started to have a panic attack.

918
00:56:28,220 --> 00:56:30,690
I broke out in a cold sweat, and I couldn't breathe.

919
00:56:31,020 --> 00:56:32,450
Dad, you went to the police station too?

920
00:56:32,990 --> 00:56:34,890
No. Me?

921
00:56:35,720 --> 00:56:36,790
Did you scam someone again?

922
00:56:36,850 --> 00:56:38,420
Hey, I don't scam people.

923
00:56:38,750 --> 00:56:40,350
If anything, I'm the one who gets scammed.

924
00:56:40,820 --> 00:56:44,290
Hey, I went there as a victim.

925
00:56:45,820 --> 00:56:46,950
Yeah, right.

926
00:56:47,790 --> 00:56:50,290
I got mixed up with some woman who dined and dashed.

927
00:56:51,150 --> 00:56:53,020
Please, just grow up.

928
00:56:53,690 --> 00:56:56,220
How could you let things get this bad?

929
00:56:56,290 --> 00:56:57,920
Can't you handle anything without me?

930
00:56:58,420 --> 00:57:00,420
How many hours was that meeting, anyway?

931
00:57:01,250 --> 00:57:02,250
I'm sorry.

932
00:57:02,790 --> 00:57:04,120
You must be exhausted.

933
00:57:04,750 --> 00:57:05,750
I'm starving.

934
00:57:10,120 --> 00:57:11,290
But something...

935
00:57:12,350 --> 00:57:13,650
feels so off.

936
00:57:14,820 --> 00:57:15,820
What does?

937
00:57:16,350 --> 00:57:17,450
The meeting today?

938
00:57:18,750 --> 00:57:20,790
No, not the meeting.

939
00:57:23,550 --> 00:57:26,620
Tuna!

940
00:57:26,620 --> 00:57:28,490
- Tuna. - Should I order some tuna?

941
00:57:31,990 --> 00:57:33,520
She must be starving.

942
00:57:37,250 --> 00:57:38,390
Hello, Mu Jin.

943
00:57:46,890 --> 00:57:48,190
Hey, drink up.

944
00:57:49,720 --> 00:57:52,050
I'm a little drunk.

945
00:57:52,120 --> 00:57:54,690
I had a whole bottle of whiskey before I came here.

946
00:57:56,220 --> 00:57:58,490
Don't you think you're overdoing it?

947
00:57:58,550 --> 00:58:00,220
I'll go get you some water.

948
00:58:00,920 --> 00:58:02,090
It's okay. Sit down.

949
00:58:02,790 --> 00:58:03,790
I'm fine.

950
00:58:07,120 --> 00:58:08,120
Hey.

951
00:58:10,790 --> 00:58:11,950
What if...

952
00:58:12,790 --> 00:58:14,620
That day...

953
00:58:14,690 --> 00:58:18,490
what if I hadn't made you eat that spicy stir-fried squid?

954
00:58:19,920 --> 00:58:20,990
And...

955
00:58:22,190 --> 00:58:24,650
what if Seo Hyun hadn't thrown such a fit?

956
00:58:28,850 --> 00:58:32,490
Would you have accepted her feelings?

957
00:58:33,050 --> 00:58:35,590
Would you have been able to make that decision?

958
00:58:38,150 --> 00:58:39,390
You wouldn't have.

959
00:58:40,390 --> 00:58:41,820
There's no way you could have.

960
00:58:42,650 --> 00:58:45,790
I know you. Ever since you were little,

961
00:58:45,850 --> 00:58:48,550
you've never once seen Seo Hyun as a woman.

962
00:58:48,750 --> 00:58:49,950
I know it.

963
00:58:52,020 --> 00:58:53,620
I will try harder.

964
00:58:53,890 --> 00:58:54,890
Hey.

965
00:58:55,290 --> 00:58:57,250
You think you can make love happen just by trying?

966
00:58:57,620 --> 00:58:58,920
What is this, the dark ages?

967
00:59:00,120 --> 00:59:01,490
Trying? Give me a break.

968
00:59:03,420 --> 00:59:05,690
I was the one who stopped Seo Hyun from leaving.

969
00:59:07,020 --> 00:59:09,920
And I made that choice of my own free will.

970
00:59:13,890 --> 00:59:14,890
But...

971
00:59:16,620 --> 00:59:19,490
lately, Seo Hyun has been so incredibly happy.

972
00:59:21,550 --> 00:59:24,890
She says she feels like she has the whole world.

973
00:59:26,020 --> 00:59:28,650
And she said that she's walking on air every day.

974
00:59:30,920 --> 00:59:32,390
And when I see that,

975
00:59:32,950 --> 00:59:36,720
I think, "So this is happiness." And I feel happy too.

976
00:59:37,750 --> 00:59:40,150
So these days, behind my wife's back,

977
00:59:40,150 --> 00:59:41,990
I find myself smiling foolishly in a corner.

978
00:59:45,890 --> 00:59:47,990
Like some shameless, crazy person.

979
00:59:50,220 --> 00:59:51,220
Mu Jin.

980
00:59:52,950 --> 00:59:53,950
Sometimes...

981
00:59:55,450 --> 00:59:57,090
I wonder if Seo Hyun and I...

982
00:59:57,750 --> 01:00:01,090
are building our happiness on your misery.

983
01:00:02,390 --> 01:00:03,920
If that's the case, how can that be right?

984
01:00:03,920 --> 01:00:07,390
I am not miserable. As I said,

985
01:00:08,120 --> 01:00:10,020
it was a choice I made of my own free will.

986
01:00:13,450 --> 01:00:14,450
Right.

987
01:00:16,550 --> 01:00:17,850
Right, well...

988
01:00:18,550 --> 01:00:19,590
Okay.

989
01:00:19,820 --> 01:00:21,120
No, I don't care anymore.

990
01:00:21,650 --> 01:00:23,220
I don't know. From now on,

991
01:00:23,290 --> 01:00:26,720
I'm just going to shut my mouth, close my eyes, and cover my ears.

992
01:00:26,790 --> 01:00:28,890
Got it? You handle everything from here.

993
01:00:28,990 --> 01:00:30,090
Since you decided this,

994
01:00:30,150 --> 01:00:32,190
you have to take full responsibility. All right?

995
01:00:32,350 --> 01:00:33,650
And another thing,

996
01:00:33,650 --> 01:00:36,790
You know how unreasonable my wife can be.

997
01:00:36,850 --> 01:00:39,150
You have to deal with her too.

998
01:00:39,520 --> 01:00:40,550
Okay.

999
01:00:40,550 --> 01:00:41,620
And...

1000
01:00:45,920 --> 01:00:46,950
Never mind.

1001
01:00:48,650 --> 01:00:49,650
I'm done talking.

1002
01:00:50,920 --> 01:00:51,920
I'm done talking.

1003
01:00:54,390 --> 01:00:56,690
The more I talk,

1004
01:00:56,690 --> 01:00:57,990
the more I feel like I'm talking nonsense.

1005
01:00:57,990 --> 01:00:59,920
I don't even know what I'm saying myself,

1006
01:00:59,990 --> 01:01:01,150
and I'm so embarrassed I could die.

1007
01:01:03,590 --> 01:01:05,320
Oh, Jang Hoon Tae...

1008
01:01:05,750 --> 01:01:07,920
I never knew I was such a pathetic person.

1009
01:01:09,450 --> 01:01:12,550
I don't know if all fathers with daughters are like this.

1010
01:01:13,150 --> 01:01:15,350
I'm done. Mu Jin, I'm going to head out first.

1011
01:01:15,450 --> 01:01:16,790
Stay seated.

1012
01:01:17,920 --> 01:01:20,490
- Clean this up and take your time. - Okay.

1013
01:01:23,290 --> 01:01:24,290
Mu Jin.

1014
01:01:24,790 --> 01:01:25,790
Yes.

1015
01:01:28,590 --> 01:01:29,820
Oh, man.

1016
01:01:31,620 --> 01:01:32,620
You're a good guy.

1017
01:01:35,150 --> 01:01:36,150
A kind guy.

1018
01:01:38,950 --> 01:01:40,450
An unfortunate guy.

1019
01:01:43,190 --> 01:01:45,220
I can't look at you any longer today.

1020
01:01:45,290 --> 01:01:47,490
Don't follow me. I'm leaving.

1021
01:01:47,620 --> 01:01:48,950
- Go on. - Get home safe.

1022
01:02:01,320 --> 01:02:03,420
Yes, I'm right outside the house.

1023
01:02:04,320 --> 01:02:05,320
Okay.

1024
01:02:06,690 --> 01:02:07,920
I got ahold of Gyeol.

1025
01:02:07,990 --> 01:02:09,350
He says he's at home with Gyu Rim.

1026
01:02:09,650 --> 01:02:10,890
She's at home?

1027
01:02:11,420 --> 01:02:13,650
Then why did she have her phone off? She had us worried.

1028
01:02:14,320 --> 01:02:15,320
Unbelievable.

1029
01:02:17,120 --> 01:02:18,120
Hold on a second.

1030
01:02:18,690 --> 01:02:19,690
Why?

1031
01:02:20,350 --> 01:02:21,950
I'll run and get some tofu.

1032
01:02:22,150 --> 01:02:23,250
We can eat it before we go inside.

1033
01:02:23,390 --> 01:02:26,650
Hey, you think this is a big enough deal to eat tofu?

1034
01:02:26,720 --> 01:02:28,720
You and Dad may be used to the police station,

1035
01:02:28,790 --> 01:02:29,920
but this is my first time.

1036
01:02:30,390 --> 01:02:32,250
You've been watching too much TV.

1037
01:02:32,690 --> 01:02:34,090
Hey, we don't have to eat that.

1038
01:02:34,150 --> 01:02:35,350
I feel uneasy. Let's just eat it.

1039
01:02:35,350 --> 01:02:37,220
You think eating it will keep you from going back?

1040
01:02:38,150 --> 01:02:40,290
Gyu Oh's right. Even if you eat it,

1041
01:02:40,290 --> 01:02:41,290
people who are going to end up back there will.

1042
01:02:41,790 --> 01:02:43,490
Look at you.

1043
01:02:43,620 --> 01:02:47,490
I heard you got into every kind of trouble.

1044
01:02:48,090 --> 01:02:50,450
Looks like it was a real circus.

1045
01:02:51,220 --> 01:02:52,650
And you are?

1046
01:02:53,590 --> 01:02:55,290
Do you guys know her?

1047
01:02:55,720 --> 01:02:57,290
I don't know her.

1048
01:02:58,220 --> 01:03:00,550
Well, I'm not interested in your private lives either.

1049
01:03:01,420 --> 01:03:02,620
The phone is turned off...

1050
01:03:02,620 --> 01:03:04,850
Why is Han Gyu Rim's phone off?

1051
01:03:05,050 --> 01:03:06,550
I need to drop my dress off at the cleaners.

1052
01:03:07,490 --> 01:03:10,090
Excuse me, sir, are you coming from our house?

1053
01:03:10,390 --> 01:03:11,390
Yes.

1054
01:03:13,620 --> 01:03:14,850
(Go We Deliver)

1055
01:03:17,350 --> 01:03:19,750
What's going on? And from the cheapskate...

1056
01:03:19,750 --> 01:03:21,290
who hated ordering delivery to save money.

1057
01:03:23,390 --> 01:03:24,550
Let's go in.

1058
01:03:24,620 --> 01:03:27,220
- It's delicious, right? - What's going on?

1059
01:03:27,950 --> 01:03:31,190
Oh my goodness. It's pork meatballs.

1060
01:03:32,420 --> 01:03:33,450
It looks delicious.

1061
01:03:35,820 --> 01:03:37,390
I didn't order any for you, Dad.

1062
01:03:38,490 --> 01:03:40,520
We can just share.

1063
01:03:41,390 --> 01:03:42,850
There's none for you guys either.

1064
01:03:43,020 --> 01:03:44,720
I only ordered enough for Gyeol and me.

1065
01:03:48,650 --> 01:03:51,290
From now on, everyone does their own laundry.

1066
01:03:51,490 --> 01:03:53,420
You can all make your own meals.

1067
01:03:54,420 --> 01:03:56,890
What are you saying? Are you trying to screw us over?

1068
01:03:57,890 --> 01:04:00,990
Whether you starve or feast, you can do it on your own.

1069
01:04:01,150 --> 01:04:03,090
As of today, Han Gyu Rim, the eldest daughter of this house...

1070
01:04:03,450 --> 01:04:04,650
hereby resigns.

1071
01:04:06,690 --> 01:04:07,890
Gyeol, go on and eat.

1072
01:04:12,350 --> 01:04:13,990
- Should we get sweet and sour pork? - Okay.

1073
01:04:14,050 --> 01:04:16,390
Resigns...

1074
01:04:17,220 --> 01:04:18,390
Open up.

1075
01:04:18,720 --> 01:04:21,820
- This is delicious, isn't it? - Yes.

1076
01:04:21,820 --> 01:04:23,450
A very long time ago,

1077
01:04:23,650 --> 01:04:25,050
I lost many things.

1078
01:04:26,720 --> 01:04:27,720
My mom.

1079
01:04:28,790 --> 01:04:29,790
My baby.

1080
01:04:30,690 --> 01:04:31,690
Kim Mu Jin.

1081
01:04:33,220 --> 01:04:35,520
And me, Han Gyu Rim.

1082
01:04:37,320 --> 01:04:39,450
I'm sorry for only telling you to endure it.

1083
01:04:40,550 --> 01:04:43,220
I'm sorry for only telling you to bear it.

1084
01:04:44,550 --> 01:04:48,320
For saying it was your duty as the eldest daughter.

1085
01:04:50,190 --> 01:04:51,720
I'm so sorry...

1086
01:04:53,020 --> 01:04:55,490
for being so harsh only to you.

1087
01:05:24,590 --> 01:05:26,450
(Love on the Menu)

1088
01:05:26,820 --> 01:05:28,250
If you think it's unfair, then leave.

1089
01:05:28,320 --> 01:05:29,820
You're going to get fired soon anyway.

1090
01:05:29,890 --> 01:05:33,120
Why is the world so unfair only to my sister?

1091
01:05:33,420 --> 01:05:35,350
That girl who dated Mu Jin...

1092
01:05:35,890 --> 01:05:37,550
Where can I find her?

1093
01:05:37,750 --> 01:05:40,720
Hee Na said she isn't interested in you.

1094
01:05:40,820 --> 01:05:42,190
Just go out with me instead.

1095
01:05:42,220 --> 01:05:43,550
I can't take this anymore.

1096
01:05:44,220 --> 01:05:46,190
Even if I’m punished for this, I can’t let this go.

1097
01:05:46,190 --> 01:05:48,050
Get a grip, Kim Mu Jin.

1098
01:05:48,820 --> 01:05:50,190
Kim Mu Jin.

1099
01:05:50,220 --> 01:05:52,650
That sounded like my name. I'm sure she called me.

1100
01:05:52,750 --> 01:05:53,950
Gyu Rim called me.

1101
01:05:54,450 --> 01:05:55,650
Found you.

